# Sync to GitHub after changes

When you finish a code change the user asked for, sync `origin` on the current branch. Do not wait to be asked again.

1. Review `git status` / `git diff` / recent `git log`.
2. Commit only the relevant project files. Never commit `.env`, `.env.server`, credentials, or local logs.
3. If you create or update a Cursor canvas, also copy the `.canvas.tsx` into `docs/canvases/` and list it in `docs/README.md` so it ships with the repo.
4. Push to the tracked remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream).
5. Reply with the GitHub repo or commit URL.

Do not `git add -i`, `--no-verify`, force-push, or amend a commit that is already on the remote.
